  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong positive bias: the model systematically overpredicts levels by ~8–15 EUR across most horizons; apply a downward offset, larger when spot/history is elevated.",
    "Missed regime shift/mean reversion: when the last-30d history shows a strong run-up into the low-80s, true outcomes mean-revert into the low-70s/high-60s, but the model keeps forecasts anchored near 80–85. Add a mean-reversion term pulling forecasts toward a medium-term anchor (~70–72) after sharp rallies.",
    "Overshoot after spikes: immediately after local highs (≈83–84), the model projects continuation/upside, while realized prices fall quickly. If recent momentum is strongly positive and price is near a local max, cap upside and bias next 1–15 days downward.",
    "Horizon-dependent error: overprediction grows with horizon (errors are smaller in the first few days, then widen notably beyond ~10–15 days). Increase the downward correction with lead time (e.g., linear ramp of the negative adjustment).",
    "Volatility/shape mismatch: the model path is too smooth and too high; realized path declines persistently. Impose a downward slope when recent history shows late-stage rally exhaustion (e.g., last 5–10 days up strongly) instead of flat-to-up trajectories."
  ]
}
